PAL.RES resource-archive member resolution FUN_0000_6250 (extender op-0x18 MAP-LOAD, the 532.pal
palette load that feeds the colormap palette-reduction).  ROOT CAUSE (runtime-proven + asm-verified vs
re_out/fist_image.bin 0x62c0/0x6314):

  6032 loads 532.pal (a MEMBER of the XOR-encoded PAL.RES archive) into the palette buffer 5598, which
  9f70 reduces into the terrain sub-palette that ac70 searches.  6250 OPENS PAL.RES fine (handle ok,
  CF=0) but then FAILS to find the 532.pal member -> 6032 returns handle 0, 5598 stays EMPTY, the
  reduction produces a zero LUT, and every colormap texel remaps to one index (uniform terrain).

  6250 reads the RESOURCE-archive header (16 B) then the directory ((count+1)*16 B) into the heap
  buffer DAT_623c via INT 21h AH=3F.  Two flat32 host-pointer bugs corrupted both reads:
   (1) EDX32 (the AH=3F buffer address, f002c) was written as SUB42(DAT_623c,0) = the LOW 16 BITS of the
       bump-alloc HOST pointer.  ext_addr() routes >=0x10000 raw but a low-16 value as a MODULE OFFSET
       -> both reads landed at the wrong flat address.  asm 62c0/6314 both `mov edx,[0x623c]` (full ptr).
   (2) The directory read COUNT (ECX32, f0028) was dropped to uVar5=0 -> 0 bytes read.  asm: 6303 inc
       ecx; 6304 shl ecx,4 -> ecx = (DAT_6240+1)*0x10 is PUSHed, and the 6313 `pop ecx` (which Ghidra
       lost) restores it as the read count.

  With the header read fixed the 'RESO'/'URCE' magic passes; with the directory read + count fixed the
  16-byte member entries populate and the XOR'd-name match finds 532.pal.

FIX (asm-verified): at both AH=3F sites write EDX32 = the full DAT_623c host pointer (not SUB42); at the
directory read write ECX32 = (DAT_6240+1)*0x10.  Class: the docs' 32-bit-flat INT-21 host-pointer
(short)-truncation + dropped-register-count gap -- shared extender FILEMGR, never exercised until the
op-0x18 map-load palette member resolution (KDV uses direct file opens, not archive members).

Cascade-only (6250 archive-member path reached ONLY via the op-0x18 mission map-load; the 19 menu/dialog
verify flows never resolve an archive member) => behaviour-neutral: verify 19/19, default boot rc=0
(KDV's direct TITLE.KDV opens do NOT take the 6250 archive path -> unaffected), mainmenu 3a6ff1c5.
